msgstr "Seguire un job {#follow-a-job}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check the status {#check-the-status}"
msgstr "Controllare lo stato {#check-the-status}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Immediately after you call `run()`, the status is usually `QUEUED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Subito dopo aver chiamato `run()`, lo stato è di solito `QUEUED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Status | Meaning |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `QUEUED` | The job waits for a compute slot. |\n"
"| `INITIALIZING` | The workflow is starting an environment with the job's compute profile. |\n"
"| `RUNNING` | The workflow's entrypoint is running. |\n"
"| `RUNNING: <stage>` | The entrypoint reported a stage with [`update_status()`](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status), such as `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU`. |\n"
"| `CANCELING` | You canceled the job, and the workflow is stopping it. |\n"
"| `DONE` | The entrypoint exited successfully. |\n"
"| `ERROR` | The entrypoint raised an error or exited with a nonzero code. See [Find the cause of an error](#find-the-cause-of-an-error). |\n"
"| `CANCELED` | You canceled the job, or it reached the [24-hour limit](#time-limit). |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Stato | Significato |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `QUEUED` | Il job attende uno slot di calcolo. |\n"
"| `INITIALIZING` | Il workflow sta avviando un ambiente con il profilo di calcolo del job. |\n"
"| `RUNNING` | L'entrypoint del workflow è in esecuzione. |\n"
"| `RUNNING: <stage>` | L'entrypoint ha segnalato una fase con [`update_status()`](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status), ad esempio `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU`. |\n"
"| `CANCELING` | Hai annullato il job e il workflow lo sta fermando. |\n"
"| `DONE` | L'entrypoint è terminato con successo. |\n"
"| `ERROR` | L'entrypoint ha generato un errore o è terminato con un codice diverso da zero. Consulta [Trovare la causa di un errore](#find-the-cause-of-an-error). |\n"
"| `CANCELED` | Hai annullato il job, oppure ha raggiunto il [limite di 24 ore](#time-limit). |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`DONE`, `ERROR`, and `CANCELED` are final, and `job.in_terminal_state()` returns `True` for them. A status loop that waits for another value, such as `SUCCEEDED`, never ends.\n"
msgstr "`DONE`, `ERROR` e `CANCELED` sono stati finali e `job.in_terminal_state()` restituisce `True` per essi. Un ciclo di controllo dello stato che attende un altro valore, come `SUCCEEDED`, non termina mai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Wait for the job to end {#wait-for-the-job-to-end}"
msgstr "Attendere la fine del job {#wait-for-the-job-to-end}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To wait until the job ends, call `wait_for_final_state()`. It returns the final status, and with `verbose=True` it prints each status change. If you set `timeout` in seconds, `wait_for_final_state()` raises a `TimeoutError` when the time runs out before the job ends. The job keeps running:\n"
msgstr "Per attendere la fine del job, chiama `wait_for_final_state()`. Restituisce lo stato finale e, con `verbose=True`, stampa ogni cambio di stato. Se imposti `timeout` in secondi, `wait_for_final_state()` solleva un `TimeoutError` quando il tempo scade prima della fine del job. Il job continua a essere eseguito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`wait_for_final_state()` checks the status after 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, and 32 seconds, and then every 60 seconds, so it sees the end of a short job within seconds and makes few requests for a long job. To check at a fixed interval instead, pass `poll_interval` in seconds.\n"
msgstr "`wait_for_final_state()` controlla lo stato dopo 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 e 32 secondi, e poi ogni 60 secondi, quindi rileva la fine di un job breve in pochi secondi ed effettua poche richieste per un job lungo. Per controllare invece a intervalli fissi, passa `poll_interval` in secondi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the logs {#read-the-logs}"
msgstr "Leggere i log {#read-the-logs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anything that the workflow writes to standard output or standard error goes to the job's logs. You can read them with `job.logs()` while the job runs, before it has a result:\n"
msgstr "Tutto ciò che il workflow scrive sullo standard output o sullo standard error finisce nei log del job. Puoi leggerli con `job.logs()` mentre il job è in esecuzione, prima che abbia un risultato:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow uploads new log lines about every 15 seconds, and one last time when the job ends or is canceled. Immediately after a job starts, `job.logs()` returns `No logs yet.`\n"
msgstr "Il workflow carica le nuove righe di log circa ogni 15 secondi, e un'ultima volta quando il job termina o viene annullato. Subito dopo l'avvio di un job, `job.logs()` restituisce `No logs yet.`\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow keeps the newest 50 MB of logs for each job, and adds a line at the top that says the logs were truncated.\n"
msgstr "Il workflow conserva gli ultimi 50 MB di log per ogni job e aggiunge in cima una riga che indica che i log sono stati troncati.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To decide what your workflow logs, see [Write logs](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#write-logs). To show only the lines that match a regular expression, pass `include` to `job.filtered_logs()`. To hide lines, pass `exclude`.\n"
msgstr "Per decidere cosa registra il tuo workflow, consulta [Scrivere i log](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#write-logs). Per mostrare solo le righe che corrispondono a un'espressione regolare, passa `include` a `job.filtered_logs()`. Per nascondere righe, passa `exclude`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get the result {#get-the-result}"
msgstr "Ottenere il risultato {#get-the-result}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.result()` waits until the job ends, then returns the value that the workflow passed to [`save_result()`](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results):\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"`job.result()` attende la fine del job, poi restituisce il valore che il workflow ha passato a [`save_result()`](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results):\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By default, `job.result()` checks the status every 30 seconds and waits with no time limit. Pass `maxwait` to limit the number of checks. For example, `job.result(maxwait=40)` waits about 20 minutes. To check one time without waiting, pass `wait=False`. If `job.result()` stops waiting before the job ends, it returns `{}`.\n"
msgstr "Per impostazione predefinita, `job.result()` controlla lo stato ogni 30 secondi e attende senza limite di tempo. Passa `maxwait` per limitare il numero di controlli. Ad esempio, `job.result(maxwait=40)` attende circa 20 minuti. Per controllare una sola volta senza attendere, passa `wait=False`. Se `job.result()` smette di attendere prima della fine del job, restituisce `{}`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check how long each stage took {#check-how-long-each-stage-took}"
msgstr "Controllare quanto è durata ogni fase {#check-how-long-each-stage-took}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.events()` lists every status and stage change of a job with its time, so you can see how long the job waited for compute and how long each stage took:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"`job.events()` elenca ogni cambio di stato e di fase di un job con il suo orario, così puoi vedere quanto il job ha atteso il calcolo e quanto è durata ogni fase:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The events use the stored status names. `PENDING` is `INITIALIZING`, and `SUCCEEDED` is `DONE`. For the QPU usage of a run, see [Find the QPU jobs of a run](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#find-the-qpu-jobs-of-a-run).\n"
msgstr "Gli eventi usano i nomi di stato memorizzati. `PENDING` corrisponde a `INITIALIZING` e `SUCCEEDED` corrisponde a `DONE`. Per l'utilizzo della QPU di un'esecuzione, consulta [Trovare i job QPU di un'esecuzione](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#find-the-qpu-jobs-of-a-run).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Find the cause of an error {#find-the-cause-of-an-error}"
msgstr "Trovare la causa di un errore {#find-the-cause-of-an-error}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When the workflow raises an exception, the job ends with the `ERROR` status. For example, run the workflow with an angle that it rejects:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Quando il workflow solleva un'eccezione, il job termina con lo stato `ERROR`. Ad esempio, esegui il workflow con un angolo che rifiuta:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The logs show the traceback:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"I log mostrano il traceback:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.result()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"`job.result()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the workflow [reports errors with `send_error()`](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), read them with `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")`, and read their messages with `job.error_message()`. For a job without reported errors, `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` returns an empty list, and `job.error_message()` returns `{}`.\n"
msgstr "Se il workflow [segnala gli errori con `send_error()`](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), leggili con `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` e leggi i loro messaggi con `job.error_message()`. Per un job senza errori segnalati, `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` restituisce una lista vuota e `job.error_message()` restituisce `{}`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: for custom workflows on Fleets, a raised ServerlessError is not recorded as an error event: only provider jobs run inside gateway/templates/main.tmpl, which calls send_error(). Custom jobs run the entrypoint directly through fleet_custom_job_wrapper.py. Confirm whether custom jobs should get the same handler, and whether error_message() should return a string instead of {}. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Manage jobs {#manage-jobs}"
msgstr "Gestire i job {#manage-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cancel a job {#cancel-a-job}"
msgstr "Annullare un job {#cancel-a-job}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Cancel a job with `job.cancel()`. The status changes to `CANCELING` while the workflow stops the job, and then to `CANCELED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Annulla un job con `job.cancel()`. Lo stato passa a `CANCELING` mentre il workflow ferma il job, e poi a `CANCELED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.cancel()` returns a message about the job and about its [linked QPU jobs](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs), which it also tries to cancel. For a running job, the workflow sends `SIGTERM` to your entrypoint. To save partial results, see [Clean up when a job is canceled](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled). If the job already ended, `job.cancel()` returns `Job already in terminal state.` and changes nothing.\n"
msgstr "`job.cancel()` restituisce un messaggio sul job e sui suoi [job QPU collegati](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs), che cerca a sua volta di annullare. Per un job in esecuzione, il workflow invia `SIGTERM` al tuo entrypoint. Per salvare i risultati parziali, consulta [Ripulire quando un job viene annullato](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled). Se il job è già terminato, `job.cancel()` restituisce `Job already in terminal state.` e non modifica nulla.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: in a live test (1 Nov 2026), a job canceled while RUNNING went to CANCELING and then DONE, with its result saved, because the entrypoint finished before the stop took effect. Confirm whether a job that finishes during CANCELING should end as DONE or CANCELED. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Find a job from a new session {#find-a-job-from-a-new-session}"
msgstr "Trovare un job da una nuova sessione {#find-a-job-from-a-new-session}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `Job` object and the workflow exist only in your current Python session. After you restart a notebook kernel, pass the saved job ID to `client.job()`, or list your recent jobs with `client.jobs()`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"L'oggetto `Job` e il workflow esistono solo nella tua sessione Python corrente. Dopo aver riavviato il kernel di un notebook, passa l'ID del job salvato a `client.job()`, oppure elenca i tuoi job recenti con `client.jobs()`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`client.jobs()` returns your 10 most recent jobs, newest first. Filter it with `function`, `status` (from the [status table](#check-the-status)), or `created_after` (an ISO 8601 timestamp), and page through it with `limit` and `offset`. To list the workflows that you uploaded, call `client.list()`.\n"
msgstr "`client.jobs()` restituisce i tuoi 10 job più recenti, dal più nuovo. Filtralo con `function`, `status` (dalla [tabella degli stati](#check-the-status)) o `created_after` (un timestamp ISO 8601) e scorri i risultati con `limit` e `offset`. Per elencare i workflow che hai caricato, chiama `client.list()`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads) table on IBM Quantum Platform also lists your jobs, with their status, compute profile, and run times.\n"
msgstr "Anche la tabella [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads) su IBM Quantum Platform elenca i tuoi job, con stato, profilo di calcolo e tempi di esecuzione.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Time limit {#time-limit}"
msgstr "Limite di tempo {#time-limit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow cancels a job that runs for more than 24 hours, and the job ends with the `CANCELED` status. During long runs, [save checkpoints to file storage](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs) so that you do not lose work.\n"
msgstr "Un workflow gestito annulla un job che viene eseguito per più di 24 ore, e il job termina con lo stato `CANCELED`. Durante le esecuzioni lunghe, [salva i checkpoint nell'archiviazione file](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs) per non perdere il lavoro.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: the timeout is measured from the job's latest event, not from its start (gateway/scheduler/tasks/update_fleets_jobs_statuses.py stop_job_if_timeout). Calls to update_status() and send_error() create events, so a job that reports stages can run longer than 24 hours. This looks like a bug; confirm the intended behavior. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshoot jobs {#troubleshoot-jobs}"
msgstr "Risolvere i problemi dei job {#troubleshoot-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Problem | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `run()` fails with `Code: 429` and `Active job limit reached.` | You reached the [active job limit](/guides/run-parameter-sweep#active-job-limit). Wait for some jobs to end, or [cancel](#cancel-a-job) jobs that you no longer need. |\n"
"| The job stays `QUEUED`, and `run()` warned that `your account, plan or subscription is blocked`. | The job does not start until the block on your account, plan, or subscription is lifted. Contact your administrator. |\n"
"| `job.logs()` returns `No logs yet.` | The job is queued or just started. Wait about 15 seconds. |\n"
"| `job.result()` returns `{}` | The job has not ended, was canceled, or saved no result. See [Save results](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results). |\n"
"| `job.error_message()` returns `{}` | The workflow raised an exception without reporting an error. Read the traceback with `job.logs()`. |\n"
"| The job is `CANCELED`, but you did not cancel it | The job reached the [24-hour limit](#time-limit). |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Problema | Causa |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `run()` fallisce con `Code: 429` e `Active job limit reached.` | Hai raggiunto il [limite di job attivi](/guides/run-parameter-sweep#active-job-limit). Attendi che alcuni job terminino, oppure [annulla](#cancel-a-job) i job che non ti servono più. |\n"
"| Il job resta `QUEUED` e `run()` ha avvisato che `your account, plan or subscription is blocked`. | Il job non parte finché il blocco sul tuo account, piano o abbonamento non viene rimosso. Contatta il tuo amministratore. |\n"
"| `job.logs()` restituisce `No logs yet.` | Il job è in coda o è appena partito. Attendi circa 15 secondi. |\n"
"| `job.result()` restituisce `{}` | Il job non è terminato, è stato annullato o non ha salvato alcun risultato. Consulta [Salvare i risultati](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results). |\n"
"| `job.error_message()` restituisce `{}` | Il workflow ha sollevato un'eccezione senza segnalare un errore. Leggi il traceback con `job.logs()`. |\n"
"| Il job è `CANCELED`, ma non l'hai annullato tu | Il job ha raggiunto il [limite di 24 ore](#time-limit). |\n"

